From 905a93e229da30c48a2b1c1fae0545d6e1c426d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niluthon <37350260+Niluthon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 13:12:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 05/13] B70-0044: input embedding table in pinned host RAM
 (B70_EMBED_UVA); swap policy defaults from an offline replay

B70_EMBED_UVA=1: after loading, the target's embed_tokens (0.59 GiB per card on Qwen3.8-Flash-Next at TP 2)
moves into the pinned arena behind a UVA view; lookups read a few KB per token over PCIe. lm_head and the MTP
draft are not touched (the draft shares the target's module). The freed VRAM holds more hot experts: on 2x B70,
144 hot instead of 136 with KV 193,412 tokens (was 173,505).

0043 swap policy: B70_MOE_HOTCOLD_SWAP_PRIOR (new, default 0.01, was a fixed 0.05) and budget 8 (was 4). An
offline replay of two agentic-coding traces gave decode cold shares of 12.2 / 15.3 % against 14.3 / 17.2 %.

Port to 0.32 (from Niluthon/qwen38-flash-tp2@e536e33, Apache-2.0, via our 0.30 carry): _b70_maybe_embed_uva(model) runs after 0.32 log_online_quantization_time and before its gc + empty_cache, so the embedding VRAM is returned there.
